        {
          "question": "q-329230",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot \\,\\,$ |  | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
          "category": "ma_capture",
