          "question": "q-332745",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$",
